<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Debre Libanos</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Debre Libanos is a monastery in the Shewa highlands north of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/addis-ababa">Addis Ababa</a>, founded in the 13th century by the saint <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tekle-haymanot-saint">Tekle Haymanot</a>. Its abbot, the echege, became the leading figure of Ethiopian monasticism. In May 1937, after the attempt on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rodolfo-graziani">Rodolfo Graziani</a>'s life, Italian troops massacred hundreds of its monks and pilgrims.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/debre-libanos.jpg" alt="Debre Libanos" width="320" height="480" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: This Photo was taken by Timothy A. Gonsalves. Feel free to use my photos, but please mention me as the author. I woul... · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Debre_Libanos_Monastery_Ethiopia_Oct19_D72_12186.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
